NOTE: 

The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.


Short description
-----------------

startup1

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 Simple shear flow
 The model is a Giesekus model
 The integration scheme is explicit Euler

startup2

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 Planar extensional flow
 The model is a Giesekus model
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

startup3

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 3D flow. uniaxial extensional flow
 The model is a Giesekus model
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

startup4, startup4log

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 3D flow. Combined shear and uniaxial extensional flow.
 The model is a Giesekus model, two-modes
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)
 Also logc-version for testing.

startup5

 Startup from zero stress of simple shear flow with the xpp model.

startup6

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 The model is a multi-mode XPP model.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

startup7

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 The model is a multi-mode PTT-XPP model.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

 Similar to startup6, but now the model is a multi-mode PTT-XPP model.

startup8, start8log

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 The model is a multi-mode PTT-XPP model.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

 Similar to startup7 (multi-mode PTT-XPP model), but now the model is 2D or
 2D axisymmetric with model=18 (four components in 2D). 
 Also logc-version for testing.

startup9, start9log

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 The model is a multi-mode PTT-XPP model.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

 Similar to startup8 (2D/2D-axi multi-mode PTT-XPP model), but now model=19 
 (three components in 2D).
 Also logc-version for testing.

startup10

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 Planar extensional flow
 The model is a FENE-P model
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

startup11

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 Planar extensional flow
 The model is a FENE-P model
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

 Similar to startup10, but now using the contravariant deformation tensor with
 a choice for all four variants of the b-formulation.

startup12

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 3D flow. uniaxial extensional flow
 The model is a Giesekus model
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

 Similar to startup3, but now using the contravariant deformation tensor with
 a choice for all four variants of the b-formulation.

startup13

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 Planar extensional or shear flow (or combined)
 The model is a Chilcott-Rallison model
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)
 
startup14

 Equilibration or start-up of flow with thermal fluctuations with a constant 
 velocity gradient using the contravariant deformation formulation.
 3D single-point calculations
 Equilibrium, shear or uniaxial extensional flow
 The model is a UCM, FENE-P or Giesekus model
 The integration scheme is forward Euler

startup15, startup15_log, startup15_b 

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 2D flow. Combined shear and planar extensional flow. 
 The model is an elastoviscoplastic model (Saramito 2009).
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

startup16, startup16_log, startup16_b 

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 2D axisymmetric flow. Combined shear and uniaxial extensional flow. 
 The model is an elastoviscoplastic model (Saramito 2009).
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

startup17

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 3D flow. Combined shear and uniaxial extensional flow. 
 The model is an elastoviscoplastic model (Saramito 2007).
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

startup18, startup18_log, startup18_b 

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 3D flow. Combined shear and uniaxial extensional flow. 
 The model is an elastoviscoplastic model (Saramito 2009).
