startup19, startup19_log

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 3D flow. Combined shear and uniaxial extensional flow. 
 Elastoviscoplastic model with Drucker-Prager plasticity (Saramito 2021).
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

startup20, startup20_log

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 2D flow. Combined shear and planar extensional flow. 
 Elastoviscoplastic model with Drucker-Prager plasticity (Saramito 2021).
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

startup21

 Startup from zero stress of flow with a constant velocity gradient
 2D axisymmetric flow. Combined shear and planar extensional flow. 
 Elastoviscoplastic model with Drucker-Prager plasticity (Saramito 2021).
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

startup22

 Startup from zero stress of a flow with a constant velocity gradient.
 Multiple continuation with a different velocity gradient to obtain
 the steady state values.
 The model is a multi-mode Giesekus model.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 Both the time-dependent and the final steady data points are output.
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

startup23

 Startup from zero stress of a flow with a constant velocity gradient.
 Multiple continuation with a different velocity gradient to obtain
 the steady state values.
 The model is a multi-mode PTT linear model.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 Both the time-dependent and the final steady data points are output.
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

 Similar to startup22, but now with a multi-mode PTT linear model.

startup24

 Startup from zero stress of a flow with a constant velocity gradient.
 Multiple continuation with a different velocity gradient to obtain
 the steady state values.
 The model is a multi-mode PTT exponential model.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 Both the time-dependent and the final steady data points are output.
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

 Similar to startup22, but now with a multi-mode PTT exponential model.

startup25

 Startup from zero stress of a flow with a constant velocity gradient.
 Multiple continuation with a different velocity gradient to obtain
 the steady state values.
 The model is an evp model Drucker-Prager plasticity.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 Both the time-dependent and the final steady data points are output.
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

 Similar to startup22, but now with an evp model Drucker-Prager plasticity
 (Saramito 2021)

startup26

 Startup from zero stress of flow with an imposed shear stress function.
 Instantaneous elasticity has been handled with a finite but fast ramp
 towards the constant stress value.
 The model is a Giesekus model with two modes. 2D flow.
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

startup27

 Startup from zero stress of flow with an imposed shear stress function.
 Instantaneous elasticity has been handled with a finite but fast ramp
 towards the constant stress value.
 The model is a an elastoviscoplastic model:
 SRM1 (Saramito 2007) or SRM2 (Saramito 2009). Single mode.
 2D flow. The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

 Similar to startup26, but now with an elastoviscoplastic model:
 SRM1 (Saramito 2007) or SRM2 (Saramito 2009). Single mode.

startup28

 Startup from zero stress of flow with an imposed shear stress function.
 Instantaneous elasticity has been handled with a finite but fast ramp
 towards the constant stress value.
 The model is a an elastoviscoplastic model:
 SRM1 (Saramito 2007) or SRM2 (Saramito 2009). Single mode.
 3D flow. The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

 Similar to startup27, but now with a 3D flow.

startup29

 Startup from zero stress of planar extensional flow with an imposed normal
 stress difference function.
 Instantaneous elasticity has been handled with a finite but fast ramp
 towards the constant stress value.
 The model is a Giesekus model with multiple modes. 2D flow.
 The integration scheme is second-order Runge Kutta (Heun)

