stresstest1

 Test for the derivative of the stress expression using the contravariant
 deformation tensor (b). 3D flow.
 The model is a Maxwell, Giesekus or FENE-P model.

stresstest2

 Test for the derivative of the stress expression using the contravariant
 deformation tensor (b). 2D flow.
 The model is a Maxwell or Giesekus.

stresstest3

 Test for the derivative of the stress expression using the contravariant
 deformation tensor (b). axisymmetric.
 The model is a Maxwell, Giesekus or FENE-P model.

stresstest4

 Test for the derivative of the stress expression using the contravariant
 deformation tensor (b). 2D flow.
 The model is a FENE-P model.

steady1

 Steady flow with a constant velocity gradient.
 Newton-Raphson iteration.
 The model is an evp model with Drucker-Prager plasticity (Saramito 2021).
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 Optional output of eigenvalues and eigenvectors of Jacobian of rhs.

steady2

 Steady flow with a constant velocity gradient.
 Newton-Raphson iteration.
 The model is an evp model (Saramito 2007, SRM1) with Oldroyd-B or Giesekus
 relaxation expression.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 Optional output of eigenvalues and eigenvectors of Jacobian of rhs.

steady3

 Steady flow with a constant velocity gradient.
 Newton-Raphson iteration.
 The model is an evp model (Saramito 2009, SRM2) with Oldroyd-B or Giesekus
 relaxation expression.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 Optional output of eigenvalues and eigenvectors of Jacobian of rhs.

steady4

 Steady flow with a constant velocity gradient.
 Newton-Raphson iteration.
 The model is an evp model (Saramito 2009, SRM2) with Phan-Thien Tanner
 relaxation expression.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 Optional output of eigenvalues and eigenvectors of Jacobian of rhs.

steady5

 Steady flow with a constant velocity gradient (2D flow)
 Newton-Raphson iteration.
 The model is an evp model (Saramito 2007, SRM1) with Oldroyd-B or Giesekus
 relaxation expression.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.

steady6

 Steady flow with a constant velocity gradient (axisymmetric)
 Newton-Raphson iteration.
 The model is an evp model (Saramito 2007, SRM1) with Oldroyd-B or Giesekus
 relaxation expression.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.

steady7

 Steady flow with a constant velocity gradient (2D flow)
 Newton-Raphson iteration.
 The model is an evp model with Drucker-Prager plasticity (Saramito 2021).
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.

steady8

 Steady flow with a constant velocity gradient (2D flow)
 Newton-Raphson iteration.
 The model is an evp model (Saramito 2007, SRM1) with Oldroyd-B or Giesekus
 relaxation expression.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 Contravariant deformation formulation.

 Similar to steady5, however using the b-formulation.

steady9

 Steady flow with a constant velocity gradient.
 Newton-Raphson iteration.
 The model is an evp model (Saramito 2007, SRM1) with Oldroyd-B or Giesekus
 relaxation expression.
 Output is the viscoelastic (polymer) extra-stress.
 Contravariant deformation formulation. 3D flow.

 Similar to steady2, however using the b-formulation and no output of
 eigenvalues and eigenvectors of the Jacobian.

